# ============================================================
# MEDIA POLICY
# ============================================================
# Optimized web assets — the files the site actually serves — stay in
# ordinary Git. They are a bounded, deliberately compressed set (~130MB
# across nine projects, desktop + mobile variants) and every deploy needs
# them, so they belong in normal history where they are diffable by commit
# and restorable without extra tooling.
#
#   public/assets/videos/work/*.mp4    <- ordinary Git (served to visitors)
#   public/assets/images/**            <- ordinary Git (served to visitors)
#
# Large ORIGINAL media — camera masters, project files, uncompressed
# exports — must never enter ordinary history. A single After Effects
# render can exceed the entire optimized set, and once committed it is in
# every clone forever. Those live under media/originals/ and are tracked
# with Git LFS, so history carries only a small pointer and the blob is
# fetched on demand.
#
# Working with originals:
#   git lfs install                    # once per machine / Codespace
#   git lfs pull                       # fetch the actual files
#   git lfs pull --include="media/originals/icekiid/*"   # or just one
#
# CI and the deploy workflow check out with lfs: false, because building
# the site only needs the committed optimized assets. Originals are never
# downloaded during a deploy.
# ============================================================

# Media only. Documentation under this path stays ordinary text.
media/originals/**/*.mp4   filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
media/originals/**/*.mov   filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
media/originals/**/*.mxf   filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
media/originals/**/*.png   filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
media/originals/**/*.jpg   filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
media/originals/**/*.zip   filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# Project and master formats, wherever they appear, are LFS by extension.
*.mov       filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.MOV       filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.prproj    filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.aep       filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.psd       filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.ai        filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.tif       filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.tiff      filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.wav       filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.aif       filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.aiff      filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.braw      filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.r3d       filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# The delivery MP4s under public/assets/ are explicitly NOT LFS — they
# stay in ordinary Git because every deploy needs them.
public/assets/**/*.mp4    !filter !diff !merge -text

# Normalise text so a Mac and a Linux Codespace produce identical diffs.
*.js      text eol=lf
*.mjs     text eol=lf
*.css     text eol=lf
*.html    text eol=lf
*.json    text eol=lf
*.md      text eol=lf
*.yml     text eol=lf
*.svg     text eol=lf
